# 20 — Design gaps
#
# What the fourteen workflows do not yet cover (DIRECTION §6), each to be
# decided as a workflow document and drawn on the canvas before it is built.

task design "Design gaps" {
  depends bootstrap.workflows

  task instruments "Workflow 15: set up an instrument" {
    effort 2d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Tunings, a second instrument, switching, the voicing rules with presets and the expert panel. Explore Chords' DESIGN §2.1, 2.5 are the guide. DIRECTION §6. Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow document and its board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/instruments.md"
  }
  task explorer "Workflow 16: the chord explorer" {
    effort 2d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "What 'Explore A on your guitar' opens: fingerings ranked and grouped by position, viewing by notation, starring a shape as my shape. Workflow 2. Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow document and its board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/explorer.md"
  }
  task leaving "Workflow 17: leaving" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Deleting an account and taking one's data out; what happens to books others are members of. DIRECTION §6. Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow document and its board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/leaving.md"
  }
  task screen_reader "How a screen reader reads a sung line" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "A decided order for chords and words read aloud, and how a chart, a diagram and a conflict are announced. DIRECTION §6. Tests: none — design deliverable (the decided reading order, in a document and on the board); shell.a11y_chart's tests pin it. Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/screen_reader.md"
  }
  task theme_picker "Draw the theme picker" {
    effort 0.5d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Decided in workflow 1 (automatic: Estante in light mode, Palco in dark); drawn on the account screen. Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow document and its board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/theme_picker.md"
  }
  task home_book_format "The home book's format" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Settings as JSON with a time on every key, so 'the later change wins' key by key; the shelf list, labels, instruments, rules, my shapes, theme, language, variation in use, transpositions. Workflows 8, 13. Tests: none — design deliverable (the format decided in a document); storage.home_book's tests pin it. Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/home_book_format.md"
  }
  task example_book "The example book's songs" {
    effort 2d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Songs written for the purpose (no one else's words), voiced for guitar, cavaquinho and ukulele, showing sections, words, variations and a setlist. Ships with the app. Workflow 1. Tests: none in code — each song and the setlist checked canonical with the cifra.md reference before it lands; account.first_run's tests pin them in the app. Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/example_book.md"
  }
  task display_preferences "Density and chord-diagram display preferences" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    note "Decide and draw two new user-chosen, synced preferences on the account screen's Preferences section beside theme and language: density (the theme.css densities, today locked at comfortable) and the chord diagram's display — left-handed mirror and vertical/horizontal neck, as Explore Chords offered — applied in the explorer and the in-song picker. Add the home-book registers to docs/home-book-format.md §4.1 and the decision to workflow 1 (density) and workflow 16 (diagram). Source: tasks/parking-lot.md 2026-10-14 (Density; Left-handed / horizontal-neck). Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow and home-book-format edits and the Theme-picker board updated)."
  }
  task recovery_email "Setting a recovery email; deleting a passkey-only account" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    note "Decide and draw where a signed-in person sets, verifies (by an emailed link) and changes the recovery email that service.email_links mails — nothing writes accounts.email today, so a passkey-only account has no recovery path. And how a passkey-only account (no email) confirms deletion: a passkey re-authentication in place of the typed email (workflow 17). Workflows 13, 17. Source: tasks/parking-lot.md 2026-10-14 (Where accounts.email is first written; Passkey-only account cannot confirm deletion). Tests: none — design deliverable (workflow 13 and 17 edits and the boards)."
  }
  task leave_book "Leaving one shared book" {
    effort 0.5d
    allocate team
    note "Decide and draw a Leave this book verb for a member who wants to drop one membership without deleting their account: where it sits in book management, its confirmation (unsaved changes and unpushed saves counted, as Remove does), and that Mine on Estante no longer offers the book afterwards. An owner cannot leave (handing ownership stays workflow 10 Later). Workflow 10. Source: tasks/parking-lot.md 2026-10-14 (Leave one shared book). Tests: none — design deliverable (workflow 10 edit and the board)."
  }
  task w07_remove_board "Draw the Remove loss-warning cases on W07" {
    effort 0.5d
    allocate team
    note "docs/mockups/W07-add-a-book.dc.html draws only the hosted-in-step Remove one-liner; add the two normative confirmations of workflow 7 L128-135 — unsaved/unpushed loss warning, and the device-only 'gone for good, download first' case — as already implemented by books.online. Publishing the canvas stays a human step (tasks/parking-lot.md, Republish the mockup canvas). Source: tasks/parking-lot.md 2026-10-14 (W07 board under-illustrates the Remove flow). Tests: none — design deliverable (the board)."
  }
}
